# Final 5-table structure

## Full table list

```text
raw_events
creators
launches
migrations
token_keywords
```

## Primary keys

| Table            | Primary key      |
| ---------------- | ---------------- |
| `raw_events`     | `raw_event_id`   |
| `creators`       | `creator_wallet` |
| `launches`       | `mint`           |
| `migrations`     | `migration_id`   |
| `token_keywords` | `keyword_id`     |

## Foreign keys

| From table       | Column           | To table     | Column           |
| ---------------- | ---------------- | ------------ | ---------------- |
| `launches`       | `creator_wallet` | `creators`   | `creator_wallet` |
| `launches`       | `raw_event_id`   | `raw_events` | `raw_event_id`   |
| `migrations`     | `mint`           | `launches`   | `mint`           |
| `migrations`     | `raw_event_id`   | `raw_events` | `raw_event_id`   |
| `token_keywords` | `mint`           | `launches`   | `mint`           |

---

# How each topic fits into these tables

| Topic                     | Table used                           |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| New launches              | `launches`, `raw_events`             |
| Creator wallet history    | `creators`, `launches`               |
| Launch time patterns      | `launches`                           |
| Name/symbol trends        | `launches`, `token_keywords`         |
| Migration events          | `migrations`, `raw_events`           |
| Time to migration         | `launches`, `migrations`             |
| Creator success rate      | `creators`, `launches`, `migrations` |
| Duplicate/repeated themes | `launches`, `token_keywords`         |
| Raw JSON archive          | `raw_events`                         |

---

# Recommended creation order

Because of foreign keys, create the tables in this order:

```sql
CREATE TABLE raw_events (...);
CREATE TABLE creators (...);
CREATE TABLE launches (...);
CREATE TABLE migrations (...);
CREATE TABLE token_keywords (...);
```

Why?

Because `launches` depends on `creators` and `raw_events`.

`migrations` and `token_keywords` depend on `launches`.

---

# Important design choice

You may notice that `launches` has:

```sql
is_migrated
migration_time
minutes_to_migration
```

Even though we also have a separate `migrations` table.

This is intentional.

The `migrations` table stores the actual event.

The `launches` table stores the easy summary.

So later you can quickly run:

```sql
SELECT *
FROM launches
WHERE is_migrated = TRUE;
```

Instead of always joining tables.

That makes your analysis easier.

